{title: Sacrifice of Praise}
{subtitle: Hebrews 13:15–16}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [Bmaj7] | [Bmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D#m]Outside the camp [C#]we [D#m]go
[B]Bearing the dis[C#]grace he [D#m]bore
No lasting c[C#]ity [D#m]here
We [B]seek the one that [C#]is to [D#m]come
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[B]Through him [C#]let us con[D#m]tinually
[B]Offer to God a [C#]sacrifice of [D#m]praise
[B]The fruit of [C#]lips that con[D#m]fess
His [B]holy name be[C#]fore the [D#m]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Do not neglect [C#]to do [D#m]good
[B]Share with others [C#]in your [D#m]days
Such sacri[C#]fices are [D#m]pleasing
[B]To the God who [C#]knows our [D#m]hearts
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Jesus suffered out[C#]side the [D#m]gate
[B]To make [C#]the people [D#m]holy
Through his own blood he cleansed [C#]us [D#m]
[B]From the weight of [C#]all our [D#m]sin
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
We have no last[C#]ing c[D#m]ity
[B]Looking for the [C#]one to [D#m]come
So we offer [C#]up our voic[D#m]es
[B]As a sweet and [C#]holy [D#m]sound
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[B]A [C#]sacrifice of [D#m]praise
[B]The [C#]fruit of con[D#m]fessing lips
[B]Always, [C#]always, [D#m]always
[B]Pleasing in the [C#]sight of [D#m]God
{end_of_verse}
